      "mathjson": -24
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "By the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus with the chain rule, the derivative is the integrand evaluated at the upper limit times the derivative of the upper limit: \\( h^{\\prime}(x) = \\left(- 4 x^{6}\\right) \\cdot 6 x^{2} \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99024",
         "rule_named": "Fundamental Theorem of Calculus with a composite upper limit"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "At x = -1 the upper limit is -2, the integrand at \\( t = -2 \\) is \\( -4 \\), and the derivative of the upper limit is 6, so \\( h^{\\prime}(-1) = -4 \\cdot 6 = -24 \\).",
         "mathjson": -24,
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99004",
         "rule_named": "evaluation"
      }
